<%# Design previews for the delight proposals. Nothing here is built or wired to data - every
    figure is a literal, so read it as a mock-up, not a component. Development only. %>
<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto space-y-6">
  <%= admin_breadcrumbs(@breadcrumbs) %>

  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "Delight previews",
                       description: "Six proposals for the student side, and two to avoid. Nothing here is built." } do %><% end %>

  <%= render "components/ui/callout",
             tone: :info,
             title: "These are mock-ups, with made-up numbers",
             body: "Every figure below is a literal in the template. Pick what you want and it gets built properly against real data." %>

  <%# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1 %>
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/card",
             locals: { title: "1. Change since last month, on the headline figure",
                       subtitle: "The portfolio value card, with a comparison line" } do %>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="tw-card p-5">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-600">Portfolio value</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 tabular-nums">$124.20</p>
        <p class="mt-1 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-medium text-green-700">
          <%= lucide_icon "trending-up", class: "size-3.5 shrink-0" %>
          +$4.20 (3.6%) since last month
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tw-card p-5">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-600">Portfolio value</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 tabular-nums">$115.80</p>
        <p class="mt-1 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-medium text-red-700">
          <%= lucide_icon "trending-down", class: "size-3.5 shrink-0" %>
          -$4.20 (3.5%) since last month
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
      <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">My recommendation: build this first</p>
      <p class="mt-1">The smallest change with the most teaching value - it turns a static number
        into cause and effect, which is the whole point of the app. Both directions are shown on
        purpose: a student whose stocks fell needs to see that too, and it must not read as
        failure. The sign and the arrow carry the direction, so it is never colour alone.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><span class="font-medium">Needs from you:</span> the comparison period.
        "Since last month" fits the monthly snapshots you already store. "Since you started" is
        gentler and never negative for a long-held portfolio.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><span class="font-medium">Effort:</span> small. Snapshots exist; this is one
        query and a line of markup. No new money maths beyond a subtraction, and it must be done in
        cents.</p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2 %>
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/card",
             locals: { title: "2. The first-share moment",
                       subtitle: "Shown once, inline above the holdings table" } do %>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-teal-200 bg-teal-50 p-5">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="grid size-12 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-white shadow-sm">
          <%= image_tag "stock_logos/KO-logo.svg", class: "size-8", alt: "" %>
        </span>
        <div class="flex-1">
          <p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-base font-semibold text-teal-900">
            <%= lucide_icon "party-popper", class: "size-5 shrink-0 text-teal-700" %>
            You own part of a company
          </p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-teal-800">You just bought 2 shares of Coca-Cola. That makes
            you one of its owners - when the company is worth more, your shares are too.</p>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="shrink-0 <%= ghost_class %>">
          <%= lucide_icon "x", class: "size-4 shrink-0" %>
          Dismiss
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
      <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">My recommendation: build this second</p>
      <p class="mt-1">"You own part of a company" is a genuine concept shift, and it lands once,
        at the moment it is true. Inline rather than a modal: a modal on a shared Chromebook gets
        dismissed by whoever walks past, and this is the one message worth not missing.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><span class="font-medium">Needs from you:</span> whether it appears once ever,
        or once per new company. Once per company is more delight and more noise.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><span class="font-medium">Effort:</span> medium - it needs a per-student flag
        to remember it has been shown, so it is a migration plus a dismiss action.</p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3 %>
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/card",
             locals: { title: "3. Your money at work",
                       subtitle: "One plain-English sentence, under the earnings breakdown" } do %>
    <div class="tw-card p-5">
      <p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">
        <%= lucide_icon "lightbulb", class: "size-4 shrink-0 text-amber-600" %>
        Your money at work
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-700">You earned <span class="font-semibold tabular-nums">$20.00</span>
        from attendance and reading. You put <span class="font-semibold tabular-nums">$16.00</span>
        into 2 companies, and <span class="font-semibold tabular-nums">$4.00</span> is still waiting
        to be invested.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
      <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">My recommendation: build this, and it is the cheapest
        of the three</p>
      <p class="mt-1">It restates numbers the page already shows, in a sentence a ten-year-old can
        read. That is not redundancy - reading "$4.00 is still waiting to be invested" is what makes
        an idle balance feel like a decision rather than a figure.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><span class="font-medium">Needs from you:</span> nothing. Every number in it is
        already on the page.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><span class="font-medium">Effort:</span> small, and no new data. Watch the
        pluralisation ("1 company") and the zero case.</p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 4 %>
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/card",
             locals: { title: "4. Personal bests, not leaderboards",
                       subtitle: "Compared against the student's own history" } do %>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="tw-card p-5">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-600">Best month yet</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 tabular-nums">+$18.40</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">March - your biggest month of earnings</p>
          </div>
          <span class="grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-amber-50">
            <%= lucide_icon "trophy", class: "size-5 text-amber-700" %>
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tw-card p-5">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-600">Reading streak</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 tabular-nums">3 quarters</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">You have earned reading money three quarters running</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
      <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">My recommendation: yes, but only ever personal</p>
      <p class="mt-1">A student's earnings come from their grades and attendance, so a classroom
        ranking publishes their school record to their friends. Against their own history it is
        encouragement; against each other it is a report card on a wall. Note the streak here is
        about <em>earning</em>, not about buying.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><span class="font-medium">Needs from you:</span> which bests are worth naming.
        I would keep it to two so it stays special.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><span class="font-medium">Effort:</span> medium - "best month" needs earnings
        grouped by month, which is a new query over portfolio transactions.</p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 5 %>
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/card",
             locals: { title: "5. Companies you own",
                       subtitle: "The logos you already ship, used as a collection" } do %>
    <div class="tw-card p-5">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-600">Companies you own</p>
      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <% %w[KO NKE F].each do |ticker| %>
          <span class="grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-xs">
            <%= image_tag "stock_logos/#{ticker}-logo.svg", class: "size-8", alt: ticker %>
          </span>
        <% end %>
        <% %w[BAC SONY VZ].each do |ticker| %>
          <span class="grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-xl border border-dashed border-slate-300 bg-slate-50 opacity-60"
                title="Not owned yet">
            <%= image_tag "stock_logos/#{ticker}-logo.svg", class: "size-8 grayscale", alt: "" %>
          </span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">3 of 10 companies</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
      <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">My recommendation: yes - this is the cheapest delight
        you have</p>
      <p class="mt-1">The ten logos are already in the repo and currently appear only as small
        row icons. As a collection they give a student a reason to look at the page when nothing has
        changed.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><span class="font-medium">One caution:</span> the greyed-out slots read as
        "collect them all", which nudges buying for completeness rather than reasoning. If that
        worries you, show only what they own and drop the count.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><span class="font-medium">Effort:</span> small, no new data. Needs real alt
        text, and the grid must wrap at 375px.</p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 6 %>
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/card",
             locals: { title: "6. Warmer empty states",
                       subtitle: "The same component, different copy" } do %>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-600">Now</p>
        <div class="tw-card">
          <%= render layout: "components/ui/empty_state",
                     locals: { icon: "chart-line",
                               title: "No holdings yet",
                               body: "Buy your first shares on the trading floor and they will appear here." } do %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-600">Proposed</p>
        <div class="tw-card">
          <%= render layout: "components/ui/empty_state",
                     locals: { icon: "sparkles",
                               title: "You have $24.00 ready to invest",
                               body: "Pick a company you know. You can buy a single share - there is no minimum, and you can sell whenever you like." } do %>
            <%= link_to "See the companies", "#", class: "tw-btn-primary" %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
      <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">My recommendation: yes, and it is nearly free</p>
      <p class="mt-1">An empty state is the one screen every student sees first. Leading with their
        actual balance makes it about them, and "you can buy a single share" removes the thing that
        stops people starting. Copy change plus the balance - no new data.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><span class="font-medium">Effort:</span> very small.</p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# ---------------------------------------------------------------- cautions %>
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/card",
             locals: { title: "Two I would not build",
                       subtitle: "Shown so the decision is explicit rather than an omission" } do %>
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-rose-200 bg-rose-50 p-5">
        <p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-rose-900">
          <%= lucide_icon "ban", class: "size-4 shrink-0 text-rose-700" %>
          Confetti and streaks on a purchase
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-rose-800">Celebrating the act of buying teaches that buying
          feels good, which is the opposite of the lesson. A daily streak makes not trading feel
          like failure - and the one thing a good investor does most is nothing. Celebrate
          understanding and earning instead, which is what previews 2 and 4 do.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-rose-200 bg-rose-50 p-5">
        <p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-rose-900">
          <%= lucide_icon "users", class: "size-4 shrink-0 text-rose-700" %>
          A classroom leaderboard
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-rose-800">Earnings here come from grades and attendance, so
          ranking students publishes their school record to their classmates. It also teaches that
          returns are a competition, when the market gave everyone the same prices that month.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# ---------------------------------------------------------------- constraints %>
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: { title: "Applies to whichever you pick" } do %>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
      <li><span class="font-medium text-slate-900">Reduced motion.</span> Any animation must be
        behind <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">prefers-reduced-motion</code>.</li>
      <li><span class="font-medium text-slate-900">375px.</span> These students are on phones and
        school Chromebooks, so every one of these has to survive a 375px width.</li>
      <li><span class="font-medium text-slate-900">Never colour alone.</span> A gain or a loss needs
        its sign and its arrow, not just green or red.</li>
      <li><span class="font-medium text-slate-900">Cents, not floats.</span> Any comparison figure
        is computed in integer cents and formatted once.</li>
      <li><span class="font-medium text-slate-900">A loss is not a mistake.</span> Prices come from
        a real API. Nothing should imply a student did something wrong when the market moved.</li>
    </ul>
  <% end %>
</div>
